Diagram: Request flow for https://www.google.com

Browser
  |
  | 1. DNS lookup — resolves www.google.com to an IP address
  v
DNS server
  |
Browser connects to the resolved IP
  |
  | 2. TCP/IP connection established, request sent to port 443 (HTTPS)
  v
SSL/TLS handshake — traffic is now encrypted
  |
  v
Firewall — allows traffic on TCP port 443
  |
  v
Load balancer — distributes the request across available web servers
  |
  v
Web server — receives the request, serves the response
  |
  v
Application server — generates the dynamic page content
  |
  v
Database — queried by the application server for the required data
  |
  v
Response travels back up the same path (database -> app server -> web
server -> load balancer -> firewall -> encrypted connection) to the browser
